The csq-socks release archives bundle two csqtt clients by amurcanov
(csqtt is developed at https://github.com/Afteroid/csqttr):

  client-2.1.9  amurcanov's 2.1.9 client, unchanged.
  client-2.5.3  the client of SanityProtocol's csqtt 2.5.3: Afteroid/csqttr main (commit 84187d6, which
                carries our upload speed fix, Afteroid/csqttr#1) plus SanityProtocol's client changes,
                source/client-2.5.3.patch: battery fixes for an idle tunnel, a downlink wake fix and
                their review fixes (offered upstream as Afteroid/csqttr#5). 2.5.3 changed the app and
                the server only; the client is the one of 2.5.2.
  On Windows: client-2.1.9.exe and client-2.5.3.exe, the same two sources built for Windows plus one
                change each, source/client-<version>-windows-bind-ip.patch: --bind-ip, which binds the
                client's own sockets to the physical network for csq-socks tun.

The Windows archive also bundles wintun.dll (Wintun 0.14.1, https://www.wintun.net), WireGuard LLC's
prebuilt and signed driver, unmodified, under its own licence: LICENSE-wintun.txt.

